      <h2>05 — Usage Guide · How It Works</h2>
      <h3>Step 1 — Setup with sitemapbuilderawfl.php</h3>
      <ol style="margin-bottom: 1rem; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
        <li>Upload <code>sitemapbuilderawfl.php</code> anywhere on your server (e.g. inside <code>/awflsitemapbuilder/</code>).</li>
        <li>Open the file in browser & log in using credentials.</li>
        <li>Use UI buttons to auto-generate <code>sitemap.php</code> and <code>list_files.php</code>.</li>
        <li>Move generated files to your website's root directory.</li>
      </ol>
      <h3>Step 2 — Building the Sitemap (sitemap.php)</h3>
      <ol style="margin-bottom: 1rem; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
        <li>Navigate to <code>sitemap.php</code> in browser → displays folders/subfolders relative to root.</li>
        <li>Select directories (file-manager style).</li>
        <li>Click BUILD → only .html files are processed, <code>sitemap.xml</code> auto-created/updated at root.</li>
      </ol>
      <h3>Step 3 — Managing with list_files.php</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>View all indexed .html files by directory path.</li>
        <li>Use <strong>Rebuild sitemap.xml</strong> button to rescan disk → stale/missing entries auto-removed.</li>
        <li>Toggle <strong>View sitemap.xml</strong> to preview raw XML. No delete button — manual deletion of entries is intentional.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

